    fork: Define usercopy region in task_struct slab caches
    =

    In support of usercopy hardening, this patch defines a region in
    the task_struct slab caches in which userspace copy operations are
    allowed. Since only a single whitelisted buffer region is used, this
    moves the usercopyable fields next to each other in task_struct so a
    single window can cover them.
    =

    In order to operate with the randstruct plugin, the usercopy region must
    stay grouped together. This is done by defining an unrandomized anonymo=
us
    struct within randomized anonymous struct in task_struct. However, since
    gcc prior to 4.6 doesn't support anonymous structs, this is marked using
    a macro as done for randstruct.
    =

    This patch is modified from Brad Spengler/PaX Team's PAX_USERCOPY
    whitelisting code in the last public patch of grsecurity/PaX based on my
    understanding of the code. Changes or omissions from the original code =
are
    mine and don't reflect the original grsecurity/PaX code.
    =

    Signed-off-by: Kees Cook <keescook@chromium.org>

